cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "security-headers: a command line grader for HTTP security response headers"
abstract: "Zero-dependency Node.js command line tool that inspects a site's HTTP response headers (HSTS, Content-Security-Policy, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy and others), grades the result from A+ to F, and reports what each missing or weak header leaves exposed. Emits table, JSON and SARIF 2.1.0 output and exits non-zero below a configurable grade, so it can gate a CI pipeline."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "TrustYourWebsite"
    website: "https://trustyourwebsite.com/eu/en"
repository-code: "https://github.com/trustyourwebsite/security-headers"
url: "https://trustyourwebsite.github.io/security-headers/"
license: MIT
version: "1.2.0"
keywords:
  - "security headers"
  - "HTTP"
  - "Content-Security-Policy"
  - "HSTS"
  - "web security"
  - "SARIF"
  - "static analysis"
  - "command line"
